WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.022 --> 00:00:03.969
- I actually think that
winters in LA are really bad,

00:00:03.969 --> 00:00:06.895
because the houses aren't insulated,

00:00:06.895 --> 00:00:09.704
so at night I have to
wear sweatpants to bed.

00:00:09.704 --> 00:00:13.622
Californians Try to Figure
Out Winter Survival Hacks.

00:00:13.622 --> 00:00:16.056
What was your harshest California winter?

00:00:16.056 --> 00:00:18.287
- The harshest winter
I've ever experienced

00:00:18.287 --> 00:00:20.632
is a sweatshirt, maybe a jacket.

00:00:20.632 --> 00:00:22.164
- It's hailed a few times.

00:00:22.164 --> 00:00:23.488
- I think one time it rained.

00:00:23.488 --> 00:00:25.786
- It's never bad, I mean
clearly, it's 79 degrees

00:00:25.786 --> 00:00:27.412
outside right now, and
I'm wearing a sweater,

00:00:27.412 --> 00:00:28.619
because I'm kind of cold.

00:00:28.619 --> 00:00:32.218
- The first time I saw snow fall in person

00:00:32.218 --> 00:00:35.283
was a few years ago in
Iceland, of all places.

00:00:35.283 --> 00:00:37.535
- I know people are going
to be like, oh Californians

00:00:37.535 --> 00:00:40.739
can't handle the cold weather.

00:00:40.739 --> 00:00:41.993
Whatever.

00:00:41.993 --> 00:00:43.577
- I can't handle the cold weather.

00:00:43.577 --> 00:00:45.503
Road Salt.

00:00:45.908 --> 00:00:47.696
- Hell yeah, I know what this is!

00:00:47.696 --> 00:00:49.089
- Salt.
- That's (bleep) salt.

00:00:49.089 --> 00:00:52.061
- I mean, I know you throw
this on icy stuff, 'cause

00:00:52.061 --> 00:00:55.567
I've seen Home Alone, and
there's the weird, like salt guy.

00:00:55.567 --> 00:00:58.191
- This helps you so you don't
slip around, break your neck.

00:00:58.191 --> 00:00:59.366
- My hand's not going anywhere.

00:00:59.366 --> 00:01:01.224
- This could be some nice traction.

00:01:01.224 --> 00:01:03.314
- It makes the snow melt.
- Yeah.

00:01:03.314 --> 00:01:04.614
- So it doesn't stay on the road.

00:01:04.614 --> 00:01:06.750
- You shovel the snow.
- You shovel the snow,

00:01:06.750 --> 00:01:09.606
and then you put this on
the ice, and it melts it.

00:01:09.606 --> 00:01:10.697
- And you just leave it for how long?

00:01:10.697 --> 00:01:12.440
- Shrinks the snow up, got it.

00:01:12.440 --> 00:01:13.747
- [Man] Your shoes get ruined.

00:01:13.747 --> 00:01:15.153
- Your shoes get ruined?

00:01:15.153 --> 00:01:16.017
That's not okay.

00:01:16.017 --> 00:01:17.688
- Did you eat it? (laughs)

00:01:17.688 --> 00:01:19.105
- Do you ever use this for cooking?

00:01:19.105 --> 00:01:21.448
- Ew.
- This goes on the floor!

00:01:21.448 --> 00:01:25.043
Tire Chains.

00:01:25.736 --> 00:01:29.219
- I have no idea what this could be.

00:01:29.219 --> 00:01:30.682
- This just looks like a death trap.

00:01:30.682 --> 00:01:31.959
- Is this for your sled?

00:01:31.959 --> 00:01:33.677
- Snow chains, right?

00:01:33.677 --> 00:01:34.908
- Or it's, like, a really cool ladder.

00:01:34.908 --> 00:01:35.930
- These are for tires.

00:01:35.930 --> 00:01:38.623
- Yeah, yeah, they're the snow chains.

00:01:38.623 --> 00:01:39.598
That's an easy one.

00:01:39.598 --> 00:01:42.036
- I assumed they were
chain chains, like, chains.

00:01:42.036 --> 00:01:42.895
- Yeah, me too.

00:01:42.895 --> 00:01:44.997
- These are like what rappers wear.

00:01:44.997 --> 00:01:46.273
- [Man] Well, there are two chains there.

00:01:47.135 --> 00:01:48.102
- Two chains.

00:01:48.102 --> 00:01:50.191
- It's like, how has
technology not gotten better,

00:01:50.191 --> 00:01:51.585
where you don't have to use these?

00:01:51.585 --> 00:01:53.465
- I mean, I have no idea how to use this.

00:01:53.465 --> 00:01:56.646
- This seems like a prehistoric
type of thing, like...

00:01:56.646 --> 00:01:58.095
- You could probably tear up
the road with these things,

00:01:58.095 --> 00:01:59.047
if you're not careful.

00:01:59.047 --> 00:02:01.694
- Like middle ages, like for your horses.

00:02:01.694 --> 00:02:03.900
- It's just a hassle,
that's just what it is.

00:02:03.900 --> 00:02:06.117
- Be careful out there, cold people.

00:02:06.117 --> 00:02:08.301
Hand Warmers.

00:02:08.301 --> 00:02:10.137
- East coast, blow on your hands.

00:02:10.137 --> 00:02:13.666
You're not going to put your
hands in fancy little pouches.

00:02:13.666 --> 00:02:15.942
- Or if I'm tired, just put a couple

00:02:15.942 --> 00:02:17.029
on my eyes.
- Oh, on your face.

00:02:17.029 --> 00:02:18.237
- Yeah.

00:02:18.237 --> 00:02:19.885
- Oh that...
- That feels great.

00:02:19.885 --> 00:02:21.862
- It's not working for me.
- I feel it!

00:02:21.862 --> 00:02:23.302
Feel this.

00:02:23.302 --> 00:02:25.252
- Oh (bleep), yours is warm.

00:02:25.252 --> 00:02:26.437
How come mine's cold?
- Because you didn't

00:02:26.437 --> 00:02:27.714
expose it to the air.

00:02:27.714 --> 00:02:30.825
- Oh, oh, okay, professional
(bleep) Californian.

00:02:30.825 --> 00:02:32.845
- If I had these on the east
coast, I would just be like

00:02:32.845 --> 00:02:34.417
heating them up and
then, like, throwing them

00:02:34.417 --> 00:02:36.040
in the snow so that it melts, cause I...

00:02:36.040 --> 00:02:38.400
- Moses, you've felt cold, you don't know.

00:02:38.400 --> 00:02:40.994
KItty Litter.

00:02:42.560 --> 00:02:43.953
- Hold up.
- So, is this a joke?

00:02:43.953 --> 00:02:45.253
- Cats pee and poop in this.

00:02:45.253 --> 00:02:47.157
- We have kitty litter also.

00:02:47.157 --> 00:02:49.502
- We know what kitty litter
is, in sunny California

00:02:49.502 --> 00:02:50.826
- We have this.
- We have cats.

00:02:50.826 --> 00:02:54.169
- Uh, uh...
- Uh...

00:02:54.169 --> 00:02:57.852
- Why would you also throw
cat litter on the snow?

00:02:57.852 --> 00:02:59.431
- Odor control!

00:02:59.431 --> 00:03:01.428
- Maybe you got some smelly snow.

00:03:01.428 --> 00:03:04.888
- Maybe your cat wants to
take a dump in the wilderness.

00:03:04.888 --> 00:03:05.738
- That's kitty litter, all right.

00:03:05.738 --> 00:03:07.433
- Oh, it's strong smelling.

00:03:07.433 --> 00:03:08.872
- Maybe when you don't
have enough money for that

00:03:08.872 --> 00:03:10.939
fancy salt you were
throwing around earlier,

00:03:10.939 --> 00:03:13.238
you gotta get this kitty litter going.

00:03:13.238 --> 00:03:15.726
- Let's see how traction-y it is.

00:03:15.726 --> 00:03:17.506
Kitty litter is used to
create traction for tires

00:03:17.506 --> 00:03:19.286
when a car is stuck in the snow.

00:03:19.286 --> 00:03:21.068
- This is not a good choice.

00:03:21.068 --> 00:03:22.809
I don't think you guys are, I don't...

00:03:22.809 --> 00:03:24.017
I think you should reevaluate.

00:03:24.017 --> 00:03:26.826
- So, do people actually,
like, have this in their trunk?

00:03:26.826 --> 00:03:27.885
- No, they don't.
- [Man] Yeah.

00:03:27.885 --> 00:03:29.093
- No, they don't.
- [Man] Yes, they do.

00:03:29.093 --> 00:03:31.299
I don't believe you, I feel
like you're (bleep) with us.

00:03:31.299 --> 00:03:33.713
- Oh, it's a thing, okay.

00:03:33.713 --> 00:03:36.084
- You guys must all have
a lot of cats as well.

00:03:36.084 --> 00:03:38.743
Could you survive a real winter?

00:03:38.743 --> 00:03:40.647
- Uhhhhh..
- No.

00:03:40.647 --> 00:03:42.644
(laughs)

00:03:42.644 --> 00:03:43.851
Oh my god.

00:03:43.851 --> 00:03:45.407
- Below zero?

00:03:45.407 --> 00:03:46.652
No, what, no.

00:03:46.652 --> 00:03:48.649
- I can't even handle lukewarm weather.

00:03:48.649 --> 00:03:50.460
- Probably like 15 minutes.

00:03:50.460 --> 00:03:52.410
- I could never survive
if my car was stuck.

00:03:52.410 --> 00:03:54.420
I would call AAA.

00:03:54.420 --> 00:03:56.000
- [Man] What if AAA couldn’t get to you?

00:03:56.000 --> 00:03:57.927
AAA can't get to, what?

00:03:57.927 --> 00:04:00.853
- I mean, I would like to
think that I would do okay

00:04:00.853 --> 00:04:03.639
in, like, Chicago, but

00:04:03.639 --> 00:04:05.892
I'm pretty sure people
are going to laugh at me

00:04:05.892 --> 00:04:07.122
once they see this video.

00:04:07.122 --> 00:04:09.165
- You should come stay with us

00:04:09.165 --> 00:04:11.023
in California.

00:04:11.023 --> 00:04:12.811
- Sunny California.

00:04:12.811 --> 00:04:15.690
- It's really nice, look behind us.

00:04:15.690 --> 00:04:17.248
I'm so sorry.

00:04:17.248 --> 00:04:19.551
 

